  "description": "A quick win: understand The Limbic System: Emotion's Home.",
  "is_free": true,
  "published": true,
  "story": {
    "hook": {
      "text": "Deep inside your brain, below the cortex, a ring of structures generates your emotional life.",
      "visual": "💍"
    },
    "buildup": {
      "text": "The limbic system includes the amygdala, hippocampus, hypothalamus, and cingulate cortex.",
      "visual": "🗺️"
    },
    "discovery": {
      "text": "It sits between the primitive brainstem and the rational cortex—mediating instinct and reason.",
      "visual": "⚖️"
    },
    "twist": {
      "text": "The term 'limbic system' is debated—some neuroscientists argue emotions aren't confined to one system at all.",
      "visual": "🤔"
    },
    "climax": {
      "text": "Regardless of labels, these structures clearly influence emotion, motivation, memory, and social behavior.",
      "visual": "🔬"
    },
    "punchline": {
      "text": "Emotion has a neighborhood in the brain. It just doesn't stay home.",
      "visual": "🏘️"
    }
  },
  "quiz": {
    "question": "Which structures are part of the limbic system?",
    "options": [
      "Amygdala, hippocampus, hypothalamus, and cingulate cortex",
      "Cerebellum and brainstem only",
      "Occipital and parietal lobes"
    ],
    "correct": 0
  },
